# oracle: minimize with fix shake "a" angle constraints on the four water molecules (w143cf_water_min.data) and
#   angle_style fourier with K = 55, C0 = 0, C1 = 0.5, C2 = 0.5: the equilibrium angle is acos(-C1/4/C2) = acos(-0.25),
#   about 104.48 degrees (src/EXTRA-MOLECULE/angle_fourier.cpp at b332f28, equilibrium_angle), in radians for fix shake
#   (src/RIGID/fix_shake.cpp at b332f28). The engine used to have no equilibrium for this style. Constraints are
#   harmonic restraints (kbond default), as in w143cf_shake_min. cg (backtrack line search) for 15 iterations.
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 2.4e-9, atoms 1.3e-8.
# oracle-inputs: w143cf_water_min.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           real
atom_style      angle
read_data       w143cf_water_min.data
pair_style      lj/cut 6.0
pair_coeff      1 1 0.1553 3.166
pair_coeff      2 2 0.0 1.0
pair_coeff      1 2 0.0 1.0
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      1 450.0 0.9572
angle_style     fourier
angle_coeff     1 55.0 0.0 0.5 0.5
fix             1 all shake 0.0001 20 0 b 1 a 1
thermo_style    custom step pe fnorm
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
min_modify      line backtrack
minimize        0.0 0.0 15 250
